## Click Dispatch

`execute_claude_action()` currently calls `human_click(gx, gy)` with its default `simple=True`, which dispatches an instant `pyautogui.click(x, y)`. The alternate human-like pattern remains available by calling `human_click(..., simple=False)`:

```python
pyautogui.moveTo(x, y, duration=0.2)
pyautogui.mouseDown()
time.sleep(0.1)   # debounce
pyautogui.mouseUp()
```

